{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014iSkfdh7kiBarzcCv8YBEb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Current Evaluation State\n     2→\n     3→## Active Text\n     4→- **Name:** cask_of_amontillado\n     5→- **Attempt:** 3\n     6→- **Phase:** awaiting_fix\n     7→- **baseline_score:** 6.10\n     8→\n     9→## Latest Scores\n    10→- Structure Detection: 9/10\n    11→- Character Extraction: 7/10 ← IMPROVED (was 4/10)\n    12→- Character Profiles: 5/10 ← IMPROVED (was 4/10)\n    13→- Chapter Summaries: 9/10 ← IMPROVED (was 6/10)\n    14→- Pronunciation Guide: 7/10 (unchanged)\n    15→- HTML Presentation: 9/10 ← IMPROVED (was 8/10)\n    16→- **Overall: 7.70/10** (threshold: 8.0) ← IMPROVED from 6.10\n    17→\n    18→## Progress Summary\n    19→\n    20→**Attempt 3 FIX VERIFICATION:**\n    21→- ✅ **Issue #1 FIXED:** \"Amontillado\" (wine) is NO LONGER in character list\n    22→- ✅ **Issue #5 FIXED:** Plot summary correctly uses \"Montresor\" as narrator (not \"Amontillado\")\n    23→- ⚠️ **Issue #2 PARTIALLY FIXED:** Montresor identified as narrator in plot_summary, BUT `is_narrator: false` in character object\n    24→- ❌ **Issue #3 UNCHANGED:** Montresor still has empty profile (NER limitation)\n    25→- ❌ **Issue #4 UNCHANGED:** Luchresi still missing from character list\n    26→\n    27→**Score improved by +1.60 points** (6.10 → 7.70). Only need +0.30 more to pass.\n    28→\n    29→## Current Issues (Priority Order)\n    30→\n    31→### HIGH (Score impact: 0.5-1 point each)\n    32→\n    33→1. **Montresor has NO profile content**\n    34→   - Problem: Montresor has empty `descriptions`, `relationships`, `evidence` arrays\n    35→   - Evidence: `characters[1]` (Montresor) shows all empty arrays, only 1 mention_count\n    36→   - Impact: -2 points on Character Profiles score\n    37→   - Root cause: NER only finds \"Montresor\" once (when Fortunato cries \"For the love of God, Montresor!\")\n    38→   - The narrator speaks in first-person (\"I\") throughout, which NER doesn't attribute to Montresor\n    39→   - Location: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` - profile generation needs narrator-aware logic\n    40→   - Fix approach: When a character is identified as the narrator (from plot_summary), build their profile from all first-person statements (\"I thought\", \"I led him\", etc.)\n    41→\n    42→2. **Luchresi missing from character list**\n    43→   - Problem: Luchresi appears 6 times in the text but is not in the character list\n    44→   - Evidence: Pronunciation guide shows Luchresi with 6 occurrences; he's a named character used in dialogue\n    45→   - Impact: -0.5 points on Character Extraction score\n    46→   - Context: He's mentioned as a rival wine expert that Montresor uses to manipulate Fortunato\n    47→   - Location: Likely filtered by mention count threshold or validation logic\n    48→   - Fix approach: Lower threshold OR investigate why a 6-mention character was filtered\n    49→\n    50→3. **`is_narrator` field is false for Montresor**\n    51→   - Problem: `characters[1].is_narrator = false` but plot_summary correctly says \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\"\n    52→   - Evidence: Inconsistency between character metadata and plot analysis\n    53→   - Impact: Part of profile score, also data inconsistency\n    54→   - Location: Narrator detection in summary agent vs character metadata\n    55→   - Fix approach: Sync narrator identification from plot_summary back to character metadata\n    56→\n    57→### MEDIUM (Score impact: <0.5 point)\n    58→\n    59→4. **Pronunciation false positives on common words**\n    60→   - Problem: Common English words flagged unnecessarily: jingled, filmy, orbs, leer, familiarly, recoiling, tight-fitting, web-work\n    61→   - Evidence: 56 words flagged total, ~8-10 are common English words\n    62→   - Impact: -0.5 points on Pronunciation score\n    63→   - Location: `src/pipeline/pronunciation/` - word frequency filtering\n    64→   - Fix approach: Add common English word list filter (as noted in ATTEMPT_1_SUMMARY.md)\n    65→\n    66→5. **\"Medoc\" missing from pronunciation guide**\n    67→   - Problem: French wine region \"Medoc\" appears twice in text but not flagged\n    68→   - Evidence: Text has \"draught of the Medoc\" and \"My own fancy grew warm with the Medoc\"\n    69→   - Impact: Minor (-0.1 point)\n    70→   - Location: Pronunciation detection pipeline\n    71→   - Fix approach: Improve foreign word detection\n    72→\n    73→### LOW (Polish items)\n    74→\n    75→6. **Fortunato profile confidence is \"low\"**\n    76→   - Problem: Only character with a profile has low confidence\n    77→   - Evidence: `low_confidence_items: [\"Character: Fortunato\"]`\n    78→   - Impact: Minor quality indicator\n    79→   - Location: Profile generation confidence scoring\n    80→\n    81→## Gap Analysis\n    82→\n    83→Current: 7.70, Target: 8.0, Gap: **0.30 points**\n    84→\n    85→To close the gap, we need approximately:\n    86→- +0.5 on Character Profiles (5→6): Would add +0.15 to overall\n    87→- +0.5 on Character Extraction (7→7.5): Would add +0.125 to overall\n    88→- OR +1 on Pronunciation (7→8): Would add +0.10 to overall\n    89→\n    90→**Recommended priority:** Fix Issues #1-3 together (narrator profile generation) as they're related. This would:\n    91→- Improve Character Profiles from 5 to ~7 (+0.30 overall)\n    92→- Potentially improve Character Extraction slightly (+0.05-0.10 overall)\n    93→- Total expected gain: ~0.35-0.40 points, crossing the 8.0 threshold\n    94→\n    95→## Fix History\n    96→\n    97→### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n    98→- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n    99→- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n   100→- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n   101→\n   102→### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fixed NER invalid name extraction\n   103→- Added check to reject names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters\n   104→- Result: Pipeline no longer fails on \"--yes\" from spaCy mis-tagging\n   105→\n   106→### Attempt 3 (2026-01-18): Added food/beverage filter\n   107→- Added `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with 24 common food/drink terms\n   108→- Pre-filter check before LLM validation\n   109→- Result: Score improved 6.10 → 7.70 (+1.60 points)\n   110→\n   111→## Output Files (Attempt 3)\n   112→- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n   113→- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n   114→\n   115→## Next Action\n   116→**Phase:** awaiting_fix\n   117→\n   118→Run PROMPT_fix.md to address Issue #1 (Montresor missing profile).\n   119→\n   120→**Recommended Fix Approach:**\n   121→The narrator profile problem requires a conceptual change:\n   122→1. When the plot_summary identifies a first-person narrator (e.g., \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\")\n   123→2. Extract that character name\n   124→3. Build their profile from first-person statements (\"I vowed revenge\", \"I led him deeper\", etc.)\n   125→4. Also set `is_narrator: true` for that character\n   126→\n   127→This is a cross-component fix involving:\n   128→- `src/agents/summary_agent.py` (narrator identification)\n   129→- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` (profile building)\n   130→- Character metadata sync\n   131→\n   132→**Alternative Quick Fix:**\n   133→If the narrator-aware profile building is too complex, focus on just:\n   134→- Lowering the mention count threshold to include Luchresi (6 mentions)\n   135→- Fixing the `is_narrator` flag sync\n   136→\n   137→This simpler fix might get us the 0.30 points needed.\n   138→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef7a1348-36ae-43ad-a27c-fe7fef12baa3","uuid":"3c8a5002-fb93-4071-868c-90ba724cb88f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","content":"# Current Evaluation State\n\n## Active Text\n- **Name:** cask_of_amontillado\n- **Attempt:** 3\n- **Phase:** awaiting_fix\n- **baseline_score:** 6.10\n\n## Latest Scores\n- Structure Detection: 9/10\n- Character Extraction: 7/10 ← IMPROVED (was 4/10)\n- Character Profiles: 5/10 ← IMPROVED (was 4/10)\n- Chapter Summaries: 9/10 ← IMPROVED (was 6/10)\n- Pronunciation Guide: 7/10 (unchanged)\n- HTML Presentation: 9/10 ← IMPROVED (was 8/10)\n- **Overall: 7.70/10** (threshold: 8.0) ← IMPROVED from 6.10\n\n## Progress Summary\n\n**Attempt 3 FIX VERIFICATION:**\n- ✅ **Issue #1 FIXED:** \"Amontillado\" (wine) is NO LONGER in character list\n- ✅ **Issue #5 FIXED:** Plot summary correctly uses \"Montresor\" as narrator (not \"Amontillado\")\n- ⚠️ **Issue #2 PARTIALLY FIXED:** Montresor identified as narrator in plot_summary, BUT `is_narrator: false` in character object\n- ❌ **Issue #3 UNCHANGED:** Montresor still has empty profile (NER limitation)\n- ❌ **Issue #4 UNCHANGED:** Luchresi still missing from character list\n\n**Score improved by +1.60 points** (6.10 → 7.70). Only need +0.30 more to pass.\n\n## Current Issues (Priority Order)\n\n### HIGH (Score impact: 0.5-1 point each)\n\n1. **Montresor has NO profile content**\n   - Problem: Montresor has empty `descriptions`, `relationships`, `evidence` arrays\n   - Evidence: `characters[1]` (Montresor) shows all empty arrays, only 1 mention_count\n   - Impact: -2 points on Character Profiles score\n   - Root cause: NER only finds \"Montresor\" once (when Fortunato cries \"For the love of God, Montresor!\")\n   - The narrator speaks in first-person (\"I\") throughout, which NER doesn't attribute to Montresor\n   - Location: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` - profile generation needs narrator-aware logic\n   - Fix approach: When a character is identified as the narrator (from plot_summary), build their profile from all first-person statements (\"I thought\", \"I led him\", etc.)\n\n2. **Luchresi missing from character list**\n   - Problem: Luchresi appears 6 times in the text but is not in the character list\n   - Evidence: Pronunciation guide shows Luchresi with 6 occurrences; he's a named character used in dialogue\n   - Impact: -0.5 points on Character Extraction score\n   - Context: He's mentioned as a rival wine expert that Montresor uses to manipulate Fortunato\n   - Location: Likely filtered by mention count threshold or validation logic\n   - Fix approach: Lower threshold OR investigate why a 6-mention character was filtered\n\n3. **`is_narrator` field is false for Montresor**\n   - Problem: `characters[1].is_narrator = false` but plot_summary correctly says \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\"\n   - Evidence: Inconsistency between character metadata and plot analysis\n   - Impact: Part of profile score, also data inconsistency\n   - Location: Narrator detection in summary agent vs character metadata\n   - Fix approach: Sync narrator identification from plot_summary back to character metadata\n\n### MEDIUM (Score impact: <0.5 point)\n\n4. **Pronunciation false positives on common words**\n   - Problem: Common English words flagged unnecessarily: jingled, filmy, orbs, leer, familiarly, recoiling, tight-fitting, web-work\n   - Evidence: 56 words flagged total, ~8-10 are common English words\n   - Impact: -0.5 points on Pronunciation score\n   - Location: `src/pipeline/pronunciation/` - word frequency filtering\n   - Fix approach: Add common English word list filter (as noted in ATTEMPT_1_SUMMARY.md)\n\n5. **\"Medoc\" missing from pronunciation guide**\n   - Problem: French wine region \"Medoc\" appears twice in text but not flagged\n   - Evidence: Text has \"draught of the Medoc\" and \"My own fancy grew warm with the Medoc\"\n   - Impact: Minor (-0.1 point)\n   - Location: Pronunciation detection pipeline\n   - Fix approach: Improve foreign word detection\n\n### LOW (Polish items)\n\n6. **Fortunato profile confidence is \"low\"**\n   - Problem: Only character with a profile has low confidence\n   - Evidence: `low_confidence_items: [\"Character: Fortunato\"]`\n   - Impact: Minor quality indicator\n   - Location: Profile generation confidence scoring\n\n## Gap Analysis\n\nCurrent: 7.70, Target: 8.0, Gap: **0.30 points**\n\nTo close the gap, we need approximately:\n- +0.5 on Character Profiles (5→6): Would add +0.15 to overall\n- +0.5 on Character Extraction (7→7.5): Would add +0.125 to overall\n- OR +1 on Pronunciation (7→8): Would add +0.10 to overall\n\n**Recommended priority:** Fix Issues #1-3 together (narrator profile generation) as they're related. This would:\n- Improve Character Profiles from 5 to ~7 (+0.30 overall)\n- Potentially improve Character Extraction slightly (+0.05-0.10 overall)\n- Total expected gain: ~0.35-0.40 points, crossing the 8.0 threshold\n\n## Fix History\n\n### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n\n### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fixed NER invalid name extraction\n- Added check to reject names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters\n- Result: Pipeline no longer fails on \"--yes\" from spaCy mis-tagging\n\n### Attempt 3 (2026-01-18): Added food/beverage filter\n- Added `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with 24 common food/drink terms\n- Pre-filter check before LLM validation\n- Result: Score improved 6.10 → 7.70 (+1.60 points)\n\n## Output Files (Attempt 3)\n- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n\n## Next Action\n**Phase:** awaiting_fix\n\nRun PROMPT_fix.md to address Issue #1 (Montresor missing profile).\n\n**Recommended Fix Approach:**\nThe narrator profile problem requires a conceptual change:\n1. When the plot_summary identifies a first-person narrator (e.g., \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\")\n2. Extract that character name\n3. Build their profile from first-person statements (\"I vowed revenge\", \"I led him deeper\", etc.)\n4. Also set `is_narrator: true` for that character\n\nThis is a cross-component fix involving:\n- `src/agents/summary_agent.py` (narrator identification)\n- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` (profile building)\n- Character metadata sync\n\n**Alternative Quick Fix:**\nIf the narrator-aware profile building is too complex, focus on just:\n- Lowering the mention count threshold to include Luchresi (6 mentions)\n- Fixing the `is_narrator` flag sync\n\nThis simpler fix might get us the 0.30 points needed.\n","numLines":138,"startLine":1,"totalLines":138}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Eje7VFrT9y2SQtn63ygjex","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\n     2→\n     3→This rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\n     4→\n     5→## Scoring Overview\n     6→\n     7→| Category | Weight | Focus |\n     8→|----------|--------|-------|\n     9→| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\n    10→| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\n    11→| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\n    12→| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\n    13→| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\n    14→| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\n    15→\n    16→**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\n    17→\n    18→---\n    19→\n    20→## Category Details\n    21→\n    22→### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\n    23→\n    24→**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\n    25→\n    26→| Score | Criteria |\n    27→|-------|----------|\n    28→| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\n    29→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\n    30→| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\n    31→| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\n    32→| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\n    33→| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\n    34→\n    35→**Checklist:**\n    36→- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\n    37→- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\n    38→- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\n    39→- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\n    40→- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\n    41→- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\n    42→- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\n    43→- [ ] \"Chapter\" vs \"Book\" vs \"Part\" hierarchy correct\n    44→\n    45→---\n    46→\n    47→### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\n    48→\n    49→**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\n    50→\n    51→| Score | Criteria |\n    52→|-------|----------|\n    53→| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\n    54→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\n    55→| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\n    56→| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\n    57→| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\n    58→| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\n    59→\n    60→**Checklist:**\n    61→- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\n    62→- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\n    63→- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\n    64→- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\n    65→- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\n    66→- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\n    67→- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\n    68→- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\n    69→\n    70→**Common Issues:**\n    71→- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\n    72→- Full names and nicknames not linked\n    73→- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\n    74→- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\n    75→\n    76→---\n    77→\n    78→### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\n    79→\n    80→**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\n    81→\n    82→| Score | Criteria |\n    83→|-------|----------|\n    84→| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\n    85→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\n    86→| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\n    87→| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\n    88→| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\n    89→| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\n    90→\n    91→**Checklist:**\n    92→- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\n    93→- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\n    94→- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\n    95→- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\n    96→- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\n    97→- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\n    98→\n    99→---\n   100→\n   101→### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\n   102→\n   103→**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\n   104→\n   105→| Score | Criteria |\n   106→|-------|----------|\n   107→| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\n   108→| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\n   109→| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\n   110→| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\n   111→| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\n   112→| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\n   113→\n   114→**Checklist:**\n   115→- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\n   116→- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\n   117→- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\n   118→- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\n   119→- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\n   120→- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\n   121→- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\n   122→\n   123→---\n   124→\n   125→### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\n   126→\n   127→**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\n   128→\n   129→| Score | Criteria |\n   130→|-------|----------|\n   131→| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\n   132→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\n   133→| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\n   134→| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\n   135→| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\n   136→| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\n   137→\n   138→**Checklist:**\n   139→- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\n   140→- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\n   141→- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\n   142→- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\n   143→- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\n   144→- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\n   145→- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\n   146→\n   147→---\n   148→\n   149→### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\n   150→\n   151→**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\n   152→\n   153→| Score | Criteria |\n   154→|-------|----------|\n   155→| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\n   156→| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\n   157→| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\n   158→| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\n   159→| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\n   160→| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\n   161→\n   162→**Checklist:**\n   163→- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\n   164→- [ ] Typography is readable\n   165→- [ ] Information is logically organized\n   166→- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\n   167→- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\n   168→\n   169→---\n   170→\n   171→## Scoring Formula\n   172→\n   173→```\n   174→Overall = (\n   175→    Structure × 0.20 +\n   176→    Characters × 0.25 +\n   177→    Profiles × 0.15 +\n   178→    Summaries × 0.20 +\n   179→    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\n   180→    Presentation × 0.10\n   181→)\n   182→```\n   183→\n   184→**Thresholds:**\n   185→- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\n   186→- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\n   187→\n   188→---\n   189→\n   190→## Issue Severity Classification\n   191→\n   192→When scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\n   193→\n   194→### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\n   195→- Character merge/split errors for main characters\n   196→- Missing major characters\n   197→- Completely wrong chapter structure\n   198→- Hallucinated content\n   199→\n   200→### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\n   201→- Missing minor but named characters\n   202→- Incorrect relationships for main characters\n   203→- Multiple chapter summary errors\n   204→- Major pronunciation gaps\n   205→\n   206→### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\n   207→- Minor character description inaccuracies\n   208→- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\n   209→- Formatting/presentation issues\n   210→- Missing some aliases\n   211→\n   212→### LOW (polish items)\n   213→- Minor wording improvements\n   214→- Edge case handling\n   215→- Performance optimizations\n   216→\n   217→---\n   218→\n   219→## Evaluation Notes\n   220→\n   221→### Use Your Knowledge\n   222→The evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\n   223→- Verify character completeness against known casts\n   224→- Check summary accuracy against known plots\n   225→- Validate relationships and aliases\n   226→\n   227→### Be Specific\n   228→Instead of: \"Character extraction has issues\"\n   229→Write: \"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\"\n   230→\n   231→### Be Actionable\n   232→Include file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\n   233→- \"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\"\n   234→- \"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\"\n   235→\n   236→### Focus on Threshold\n   237→If score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\n   238→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef7a1348-36ae-43ad-a27c-fe7fef12baa3","uuid":"1854223e-38c3-4cfd-a5cf-055a058d09bd","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/spec/output_quality.md","content":"# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\n\nThis rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\n\n## Scoring Overview\n\n| Category | Weight | Focus |\n|----------|--------|-------|\n| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\n| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\n| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\n| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\n| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\n| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\n\n**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\n\n---\n\n## Category Details\n\n### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\n| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\n| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\n- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\n- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\n- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\n- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\n- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\n- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\n- [ ] \"Chapter\" vs \"Book\" vs \"Part\" hierarchy correct\n\n---\n\n### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\n| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\n| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\n- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\n- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\n- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\n- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\n- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\n- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\n- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\n\n**Common Issues:**\n- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\n- Full names and nicknames not linked\n- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\n- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\n\n---\n\n### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\n| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\n| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\n- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\n- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\n- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\n- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\n- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\n\n---\n\n### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\n| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\n| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\n- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\n- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\n- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\n- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\n- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\n- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\n\n---\n\n### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\n| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\n| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\n- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\n- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\n- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\n- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\n- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\n- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\n\n---\n\n### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\n| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\n| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\n- [ ] Typography is readable\n- [ ] Information is logically organized\n- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\n- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\n\n---\n\n## Scoring Formula\n\n```\nOverall = (\n    Structure × 0.20 +\n    Characters × 0.25 +\n    Profiles × 0.15 +\n    Summaries × 0.20 +\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\n    Presentation × 0.10\n)\n```\n\n**Thresholds:**\n- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\n- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\n\n---\n\n## Issue Severity Classification\n\nWhen scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\n\n### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\n- Character merge/split errors for main characters\n- Missing major characters\n- Completely wrong chapter structure\n- Hallucinated content\n\n### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\n- Missing minor but named characters\n- Incorrect relationships for main characters\n- Multiple chapter summary errors\n- Major pronunciation gaps\n\n### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\n- Minor character description inaccuracies\n- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\n- Formatting/presentation issues\n- Missing some aliases\n\n### LOW (polish items)\n- Minor wording improvements\n- Edge case handling\n- Performance optimizations\n\n---\n\n## Evaluation Notes\n\n### Use Your Knowledge\nThe evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\n- Verify character completeness against known casts\n- Check summary accuracy against known plots\n- Validate relationships and aliases\n\n### Be Specific\nInstead of: \"Character extraction has issues\"\nWrite: \"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\"\n\n### Be Actionable\nInclude file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\n- \"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\"\n- \"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\"\n\n### Focus on Threshold\nIf score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\n","numLines":238,"startLine":1,"totalLines":238}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5yc2KNDPDKMeKWuJnLNpR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Audiobook Agent - Operational Guide\n     2→\n     3→This guide provides operational commands and codebase navigation for the autonomous improvement loop.\n     4→\n     5→## Running the Analysis Pipeline\n     6→\n     7→### Basic Commands\n     8→\n     9→```bash\n    10→# Full analysis on a text file with HTML output (use --rich-progress for live updates)\n    11→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --html output/gatsby/report.html --output output/gatsby/analysis.json --rich-progress\n    12→\n    13→# With specific models per agent\n    14→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt \\\n    15→    --structure-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    16→    --character-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    17→    --summary-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    18→    --pronunciation-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    19→    --html output/gatsby/report.html \\\n    20→    --rich-progress\n    21→\n    22→# Set default model for all agents\n    23→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --llm-model qwen2.5:32b --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n    24→\n    25→# Adjust minimum character mentions threshold\n    26→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --min-mentions 3 --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n    27→```\n    28→\n    29→### CLI Options\n    30→\n    31→| Option | Description | Default |\n    32→|--------|-------------|---------|\n    33→| `--output FILE` | JSON output path | `{input_stem}.analysis.json` |\n    34→| `--html FILE` | HTML report path | None |\n    35→| `--tui` | Open interactive TUI after analysis | False |\n    36→| `--wpm N` | Words per minute for duration estimates | 150 |\n    37→| `--min-mentions N` | Minimum character mentions to include | 2 |\n    38→| `--llm-model MODEL` | Default model for all agents | System default |\n    39→| `--structure-model MODEL` | Model for chapter detection | Default |\n    40→| `--character-model MODEL` | Model for character extraction | Default |\n    41→| `--summary-model MODEL` | Model for chapter summaries | Default |\n    42→| `--pronunciation-model MODEL` | Model for pronunciation flags | Default |\n    43→| `--rich-progress` | Show live-updating progress display | False |\n    44→\n    45→## Output Locations\n    46→\n    47→```\n    48→output/\n    49→└── {book_name}/\n    50→    ├── report.html          # HTML report for narrator prep\n    51→    └── analysis.json        # Full JSON analysis data\n    52→```\n    53→\n    54→## Test Texts\n    55→\n    56→Available in `Test_Texts/`:\n    57→- `gatsby.txt` - The Great Gatsby (306 KB)\n    58→- `Frankenstein_ebook.txt` - Frankenstein (421 KB)\n    59→- `East of Eden - East Of Eden.pdf` - East of Eden (1.6 MB)\n    60→- `I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream.pdf` - Ellison short story (325 KB)\n    61→- `One Hundred Years of Solitude - One_Hundred_Years_of_Solitude.pdf` - Marquez (1.5 MB)\n    62→- `See the Light V-15 11-11-25.docx` - Test document (1.2 MB)\n    63→\n    64→## Key Source Files\n    65→\n    66→### Agent System\n    67→| File | Purpose |\n    68→|------|---------|\n    69→| `src/agents/base.py` | Abstract Agent class with verify/refine methods |\n    70→| `src/agents/structure.py` | StructureAgent - chapter detection |\n    71→| `src/agents/characters.py` | CharacterAgent - character extraction & aliases |\n    72→| `src/agents/summaries.py` | SummaryAgent - chapter summaries |\n    73→| `src/agents/pronunciation.py` | PronunciationAgent - pronunciation flags |\n    74→| `src/agents/config.py` | OrchestratorConfig, per-agent model settings |\n    75→| `src/agents/validation.py` | Upstream validation types |\n    76→\n    77→### Pipeline\n    78→| File | Purpose |\n    79→|------|---------|\n    80→| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents |\n    81→| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` | Character NER and extraction |\n    82→| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/` | Character profile generation |\n    83→| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client (Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic) |\n    84→| `src/pipeline/metrics.py` | Profiling and metrics |\n    85→\n    86→### Entry Points\n    87→| File | Purpose |\n    88→|------|---------|\n    89→| `src/cli.py` | CLI entry point (`audiobook-prep`) |\n    90→| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI |\n    91→| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI |\n    92→\n    93→### Data Models\n    94→| File | Purpose |\n    95→|------|---------|\n    96→| `src/models.py` | Core Pydantic models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\n    97→| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/models.py` | Character extraction models |\n    98→| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/models.py` | Character profiling models |\n    99→\n   100→## Configuration\n   101→\n   102→### Agent Model Recommendations\n   103→\n   104→From `src/agents/config.py`:\n   105→\n   106→```python\n   107→RECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS = {\n   108→    \"structure\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:7b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n   109→    \"characters\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n   110→    \"summaries\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n   111→    \"pronunciation\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:32b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n   112→}\n   113→```\n   114→\n   115→### Verification Levels\n   116→\n   117→Agents support three verification levels:\n   118→- `STRUCTURAL` - Fast heuristic checks, no LLM\n   119→- `SELF_CHECK` - Local LLM validation, book-agnostic\n   120→- `ORACLE` - Claude-assisted (used by this improvement loop)\n   121→\n   122→## Common Issues & Fixes\n   123→\n   124→### Ollama Connection\n   125→```bash\n   126→# Ensure Ollama is running\n   127→ollama serve\n   128→\n   129→# Check available models\n   130→ollama list\n   131→\n   132→# Pull a model if needed\n   133→ollama pull qwen2.5:32b\n   134→```\n   135→\n   136→### Out of Memory\n   137→- Reduce model size: Use 14b instead of 32b\n   138→- Process shorter texts first\n   139→- Check GPU memory: `nvidia-smi`\n   140→\n   141→### Slow Analysis\n   142→- Full analysis of a novel can take 10-60 minutes\n   143→- Use smaller models for faster iteration during development\n   144→- Check `output/{book}/pipeline.log` for progress\n   145→\n   146→## Testing\n   147→\n   148→```bash\n   149→# Run all tests\n   150→pytest tests/ -v\n   151→\n   152→# Run specific agent tests\n   153→pytest tests/test_character_agent.py -v\n   154→pytest tests/test_structure_agent.py -v\n   155→pytest tests/test_summary_agent.py -v\n   156→pytest tests/test_pronunciation_agent.py -v\n   157→\n   158→# Run alias/merging tests\n   159→pytest tests/test_alias_merging.py -v\n   160→pytest tests/test_coreference.py -v\n   161→\n   162→# Run with coverage\n   163→pytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\n   164→```\n   165→\n   166→## Loop-Specific Files\n   167→\n   168→| File | Purpose |\n   169→|------|---------|\n   170→| `oracle-loop.sh` | Bash orchestrator for the improvement loop |\n   171→| `PROMPT_analyze.md` | Phase 1 instructions |\n   172→| `PROMPT_evaluate.md` | Phase 2 oracle evaluation instructions |\n   173→| `PROMPT_fix.md` | Phase 3 fix instructions |\n   174→| `manifest.json` | Test text tracking |\n   175→| `EVALUATION_STATE.md` | Current state and issues |\n   176→| `spec/output_quality.md` | Quality evaluation rubric |\n   177→| `logs/` | Iteration logs |\n   178→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef7a1348-36ae-43ad-a27c-fe7fef12baa3","uuid":"1cc9f640-4665-4a76-839c-663fb80732bb","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/AGENTS.md","content":"# Audiobook Agent - Operational Guide\n\nThis guide provides operational commands and codebase navigation for the autonomous improvement loop.\n\n## Running the Analysis Pipeline\n\n### Basic Commands\n\n```bash\n# Full analysis on a text file with HTML output (use --rich-progress for live updates)\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --html output/gatsby/report.html --output output/gatsby/analysis.json --rich-progress\n\n# With specific models per agent\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt \\\n    --structure-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    --character-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    --summary-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    --pronunciation-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    --html output/gatsby/report.html \\\n    --rich-progress\n\n# Set default model for all agents\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --llm-model qwen2.5:32b --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n\n# Adjust minimum character mentions threshold\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --min-mentions 3 --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n```\n\n### CLI Options\n\n| Option | Description | Default |\n|--------|-------------|---------|\n| `--output FILE` | JSON output path | `{input_stem}.analysis.json` |\n| `--html FILE` | HTML report path | None |\n| `--tui` | Open interactive TUI after analysis | False |\n| `--wpm N` | Words per minute for duration estimates | 150 |\n| `--min-mentions N` | Minimum character mentions to include | 2 |\n| `--llm-model MODEL` | Default model for all agents | System default |\n| `--structure-model MODEL` | Model for chapter detection | Default |\n| `--character-model MODEL` | Model for character extraction | Default |\n| `--summary-model MODEL` | Model for chapter summaries | Default |\n| `--pronunciation-model MODEL` | Model for pronunciation flags | Default |\n| `--rich-progress` | Show live-updating progress display | False |\n\n## Output Locations\n\n```\noutput/\n└── {book_name}/\n    ├── report.html          # HTML report for narrator prep\n    └── analysis.json        # Full JSON analysis data\n```\n\n## Test Texts\n\nAvailable in `Test_Texts/`:\n- `gatsby.txt` - The Great Gatsby (306 KB)\n- `Frankenstein_ebook.txt` - Frankenstein (421 KB)\n- `East of Eden - East Of Eden.pdf` - East of Eden (1.6 MB)\n- `I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream.pdf` - Ellison short story (325 KB)\n- `One Hundred Years of Solitude - One_Hundred_Years_of_Solitude.pdf` - Marquez (1.5 MB)\n- `See the Light V-15 11-11-25.docx` - Test document (1.2 MB)\n\n## Key Source Files\n\n### Agent System\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/agents/base.py` | Abstract Agent class with verify/refine methods |\n| `src/agents/structure.py` | StructureAgent - chapter detection |\n| `src/agents/characters.py` | CharacterAgent - character extraction & aliases |\n| `src/agents/summaries.py` | SummaryAgent - chapter summaries |\n| `src/agents/pronunciation.py` | PronunciationAgent - pronunciation flags |\n| `src/agents/config.py` | OrchestratorConfig, per-agent model settings |\n| `src/agents/validation.py` | Upstream validation types |\n\n### Pipeline\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents |\n| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` | Character NER and extraction |\n| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/` | Character profile generation |\n| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client (Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic) |\n| `src/pipeline/metrics.py` | Profiling and metrics |\n\n### Entry Points\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/cli.py` | CLI entry point (`audiobook-prep`) |\n| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI |\n| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI |\n\n### Data Models\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/models.py` | Core Pydantic models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\n| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/models.py` | Character extraction models |\n| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/models.py` | Character profiling models |\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Agent Model Recommendations\n\nFrom `src/agents/config.py`:\n\n```python\nRECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS = {\n    \"structure\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:7b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n    \"characters\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n    \"summaries\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n    \"pronunciation\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:32b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n}\n```\n\n### Verification Levels\n\nAgents support three verification levels:\n- `STRUCTURAL` - Fast heuristic checks, no LLM\n- `SELF_CHECK` - Local LLM validation, book-agnostic\n- `ORACLE` - Claude-assisted (used by this improvement loop)\n\n## Common Issues & Fixes\n\n### Ollama Connection\n```bash\n# Ensure Ollama is running\nollama serve\n\n# Check available models\nollama list\n\n# Pull a model if needed\nollama pull qwen2.5:32b\n```\n\n### Out of Memory\n- Reduce model size: Use 14b instead of 32b\n- Process shorter texts first\n- Check GPU memory: `nvidia-smi`\n\n### Slow Analysis\n- Full analysis of a novel can take 10-60 minutes\n- Use smaller models for faster iteration during development\n- Check `output/{book}/pipeline.log` for progress\n\n## Testing\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\npytest tests/ -v\n\n# Run specific agent tests\npytest tests/test_character_agent.py -v\npytest tests/test_structure_agent.py -v\npytest tests/test_summary_agent.py -v\npytest tests/test_pronunciation_agent.py -v\n\n# Run alias/merging tests\npytest tests/test_alias_merging.py -v\npytest tests/test_coreference.py -v\n\n# Run with coverage\npytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\n```\n\n## Loop-Specific Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `oracle-loop.sh` | Bash orchestrator for the improvement loop |\n| `PROMPT_analyze.md` | Phase 1 instructions |\n| `PROMPT_evaluate.md` | Phase 2 oracle evaluation instructions |\n| `PROMPT_fix.md` | Phase 3 fix instructions |\n| `manifest.json` | Test text tracking |\n| `EVALUATION_STATE.md` | Current state and issues |\n| `spec/output_quality.md` | Quality evaluation rubric |\n| `logs/` | Iteration logs |\n","numLines":178,"startLine":1,"totalLines":178}}}
