{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YFFRqAprcoFTjn56HfqWEy","type":"tool_result","content":"   131→    def identify_characters(\n   132→        self,\n   133→        chapter_summaries: list[ChapterSummary],\n   134→        plot_summary: str,\n   135→    ) -> tuple[list[IdentifiedCharacter], Optional[str], str]:\n   136→        \"\"\"\n   137→        Extract characters from summaries.\n   138→\n   139→        The LLM has already done the hard work of understanding\n   140→        who is who in the chapter summaries. We extract and unify here.\n   141→\n   142→        Args:\n   143→            chapter_summaries: List of chapter summaries\n   144→            plot_summary: Overall plot summary\n   145→\n   146→        Returns:\n   147→            Tuple of (characters, narrator_name, narrative_style)\n   148→        \"\"\"\n   149→        # Build summaries text\n   150→        summaries_text = self._format_summaries(chapter_summaries)\n   151→\n   152→        prompt = CHARACTER_IDENTIFICATION_PROMPT.format(\n   153→            chapter_summaries=summaries_text,\n   154→            plot_summary=plot_summary or \"No plot summary available.\",\n   155→        )\n   156→\n   157→        result, response = self.llm.query_json(prompt, system=CHARACTER_IDENTIFICATION_SYSTEM)\n   158→\n   159→        if not response.success or result is None:\n   160→            logger.error(f\"Character identification failed: {response.error}\")\n   161→            # Fall back to extracting characters directly from summaries\n   162→            return self._fallback_extraction(chapter_summaries), None, \"unknown\"\n   163→\n   164→        # Parse the response\n   165→        characters = self._parse_character_list(result, chapter_summaries)\n   166→\n   167→        # Extract narrator info\n   168→        narrator_info = result.get(\"narrator\", {})\n   169→        narrator_name = narrator_info.get(\"name\") if narrator_info else None\n   170→        narrative_style = narrator_info.get(\"narrative_style\", \"unknown\") if narrator_info else \"unknown\"\n   171→\n   172→        # Mark the narrator in the character list\n   173→        if narrator_name:\n   174→            for char in characters:\n   175→                if char.canonical_name.lower() == narrator_name.lower():\n   176→                    char.is_narrator = True\n   177→                    char.narrative_role = narrator_info.get(\"role\", \"Narrator\")\n   178→                    break\n   179→                # Also check aliases\n   180→                if any(alias.lower() == narrator_name.lower() for alias in char.aliases):\n   181→                    char.is_narrator = True\n   182→                    char.narrative_role = narrator_info.get(\"role\", \"Narrator\")\n   183→                    break\n   184→\n   185→        logger.info(f\"Identified {len(characters)} characters from summaries\")\n   186→        if narrator_name:\n   187→            logger.info(f\"Narrator: {narrator_name} ({narrative_style})\")\n   188→\n   189→        return characters, narrator_name, narrative_style\n   190→\n   191→    def _format_summaries(self, chapter_summaries: list[ChapterSummary]) -> str:\n   192→        \"\"\"Format chapter summaries for the prompt.\"\"\"\n   193→        lines = []\n   194→        for summary in chapter_summaries:\n   195→            title = summary.chapter_title or f\"Chapter {summary.chapter_index}\"\n   196→            lines.append(f\"Chapter {summary.chapter_index} ({title}):\")\n   197→            lines.append(f\"  Summary: {summary.summary}\")\n   198→            if summary.characters_present:\n   199→                lines.append(f\"  Characters: {', '.join(summary.characters_present)}\")\n   200→            lines.append(\"\")\n   201→        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n   202→\n   203→    def _parse_character_list(\n   204→        self,\n   205→        result: dict,\n   206→        chapter_summaries: list[ChapterSummary],\n   207→    ) -> list[IdentifiedCharacter]:\n   208→        \"\"\"Parse LLM response into IdentifiedCharacter objects.\"\"\"\n   209→        characters = []\n   210→        seen_names = set()  # Track seen names to avoid duplicates\n   211→\n   212→        for char_data in result.get(\"characters\", []):\n   213→            canonical = char_data.get(\"canonical_name\", \"\").strip()\n   214→            if not canonical:\n   215→                continue\n   216→\n   217→            # Skip if we've already seen this character\n   218→            canonical_lower = canonical.lower()\n   219→            if canonical_lower in seen_names:\n   220→                continue\n   221→            seen_names.add(canonical_lower)\n   222→\n   223→            # Also add aliases to seen set\n   224→            aliases = [a.strip() for a in char_data.get(\"aliases\", []) if a.strip()]\n   225→            for alias in aliases:\n   226→                seen_names.add(alias.lower())\n   227→\n   228→            # Determine role\n   229→            role_str = char_data.get(\"role\", \"supporting\").lower()\n   230→            if role_str not in (\"protagonist\", \"antagonist\", \"supporting\", \"minor\"):\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef7a1348-36ae-43ad-a27c-fe7fef12baa3","uuid":"2f072882-a5b0-4b0e-a691-7361a20c8975","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_profiling/identifier.py","content":"    def identify_characters(\n        self,\n        chapter_summaries: list[ChapterSummary],\n        plot_summary: str,\n    ) -> tuple[list[IdentifiedCharacter], Optional[str], str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Extract characters from summaries.\n\n        The LLM has already done the hard work of understanding\n        who is who in the chapter summaries. We extract and unify here.\n\n        Args:\n            chapter_summaries: List of chapter summaries\n            plot_summary: Overall plot summary\n\n        Returns:\n            Tuple of (characters, narrator_name, narrative_style)\n        \"\"\"\n        # Build summaries text\n        summaries_text = self._format_summaries(chapter_summaries)\n\n        prompt = CHARACTER_IDENTIFICATION_PROMPT.format(\n            chapter_summaries=summaries_text,\n            plot_summary=plot_summary or \"No plot summary available.\",\n        )\n\n        result, response = self.llm.query_json(prompt, system=CHARACTER_IDENTIFICATION_SYSTEM)\n\n        if not response.success or result is None:\n            logger.error(f\"Character identification failed: {response.error}\")\n            # Fall back to extracting characters directly from summaries\n            return self._fallback_extraction(chapter_summaries), None, \"unknown\"\n\n        # Parse the response\n        characters = self._parse_character_list(result, chapter_summaries)\n\n        # Extract narrator info\n        narrator_info = result.get(\"narrator\", {})\n        narrator_name = narrator_info.get(\"name\") if narrator_info else None\n        narrative_style = narrator_info.get(\"narrative_style\", \"unknown\") if narrator_info else \"unknown\"\n\n        # Mark the narrator in the character list\n        if narrator_name:\n            for char in characters:\n                if char.canonical_name.lower() == narrator_name.lower():\n                    char.is_narrator = True\n                    char.narrative_role = narrator_info.get(\"role\", \"Narrator\")\n                    break\n                # Also check aliases\n                if any(alias.lower() == narrator_name.lower() for alias in char.aliases):\n                    char.is_narrator = True\n                    char.narrative_role = narrator_info.get(\"role\", \"Narrator\")\n                    break\n\n        logger.info(f\"Identified {len(characters)} characters from summaries\")\n        if narrator_name:\n            logger.info(f\"Narrator: {narrator_name} ({narrative_style})\")\n\n        return characters, narrator_name, narrative_style\n\n    def _format_summaries(self, chapter_summaries: list[ChapterSummary]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Format chapter summaries for the prompt.\"\"\"\n        lines = []\n        for summary in chapter_summaries:\n            title = summary.chapter_title or f\"Chapter {summary.chapter_index}\"\n            lines.append(f\"Chapter {summary.chapter_index} ({title}):\")\n            lines.append(f\"  Summary: {summary.summary}\")\n            if summary.characters_present:\n                lines.append(f\"  Characters: {', '.join(summary.characters_present)}\")\n            lines.append(\"\")\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n    def _parse_character_list(\n        self,\n        result: dict,\n        chapter_summaries: list[ChapterSummary],\n    ) -> list[IdentifiedCharacter]:\n        \"\"\"Parse LLM response into IdentifiedCharacter objects.\"\"\"\n        characters = []\n        seen_names = set()  # Track seen names to avoid duplicates\n\n        for char_data in result.get(\"characters\", []):\n            canonical = char_data.get(\"canonical_name\", \"\").strip()\n            if not canonical:\n                continue\n\n            # Skip if we've already seen this character\n            canonical_lower = canonical.lower()\n            if canonical_lower in seen_names:\n                continue\n            seen_names.add(canonical_lower)\n\n            # Also add aliases to seen set\n            aliases = [a.strip() for a in char_data.get(\"aliases\", []) if a.strip()]\n            for alias in aliases:\n                seen_names.add(alias.lower())\n\n            # Determine role\n            role_str = char_data.get(\"role\", \"supporting\").lower()\n            if role_str not in (\"protagonist\", \"antagonist\", \"supporting\", \"minor\"):","numLines":100,"startLine":131,"totalLines":342}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01V7D7EibTaWyxH85nYH9NVu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I found it. Lines 173-183 show that the identifier DOES set `is_narrator = True` when it finds the narrator. But the problem is it's doing a name match: `if char.canonical_name.lower() == narrator_name.lower()`.\n\n### Issue #3: is_narrator flag mismatch - ROOT CAUSE FOUND\n\n**Data flow trace:**\n1. **Symptom:** `characters[1].is_narrator = false` for Montresor in analysis.json\n2. **Narrator detection works:** plot_summary says \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\"  \n3. **Flag should be set:** `identifier.identify_characters()` at lines 173-183 sets `is_narrator=True` when name matches\n4. **Root cause:** The character profiling pipeline identifies characters from chapter summaries, and the narrator name from the plot summary. But if \"Montresor\" isn't mentioned in chapter summaries (because he narrates as \"I\"), the identifier won't create a character entry for him, so there's no character to mark as narrator.\n\nWait, let me verify this. Looking back at the JSON, Montresor IS in the character list (line 57). So the identifier DID create a character for Montresor. Let me check if the name match is failing:\n\n**Actually, looking more carefully:** The identifier extracts `narrator_name` from `result.get(\"narrator\", {})` (line 169). This comes from the LLM's JSON response. Then it searches for that name in the characters list (lines 174-183) and sets `is_narrator=True`. \n\nThe issue must be that either:\n1. The LLM didn't return the narrator name in the expected format, OR\n2. The name matching failed (e.g., LLM said \"Montresor\" but character is stored with different casing/spelling)\n\nLet me check the profiling pipeline to see if there's logging I can examine. Actually, let me just check if this is a simple case of the two pipelines being disconnected. Let me see where Characters come from in the final output - are they from character_extraction or character_profiling?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1553,"cache_read_input_tokens":89030,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1553,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef7a1348-36ae-43ad-a27c-fe7fef12baa3","uuid":"3d2b7e7b-a166-4b0d-b0d9-ca1b5f1471f5"}
